<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Lüneburg Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1371">1371</a>–<a href="/years/1388">1388</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a> Succession was fought from 1371 to 1388 after Duke William II of Lüneburg died without sons. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Emperor Charles IV</a> granted the principality to the Ascanian dukes of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>, while the Guelph dukes of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> claimed it by inheritance. The town of Lüneburg sided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ascania">Ascanians</a> and destroyed the ducal castle. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Guelphs</a> prevailed after the Battle of Winsen in 1388.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-luneburg-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Lüneburg Succession" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DEU_Fuerstentum_Lueneburg_COA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
